WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
Ben Francis built Gymshark into a

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:05.640
billion-dollar brand, but what you might

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.640
not know is it was started with a £3.50

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.320
website selling supplements while he

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.840
worked at Pizza [music] Hut. So, I sat

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.760
down with Ben to break down the eight

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.520
lessons he's learned along the way from

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.560
finding your first idea to building a

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.440
business that can grow beyond you. And

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.000
if you're wondering where to start, his

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.560
first lesson might take [music] some of

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.400
the pressure off. I'd like to just go

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.040
back to the beginning story. I still

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.600
don't think people understand [music]

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.680
what's happened. They see the headlines,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.360
kid worked at Pizza Hut, saved up some

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.320
money, and and started a clothing brand.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.480
But, I think one of the things I've

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.400
always found interesting about your

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.920
story that people don't know is that you

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.320
started many other businesses as well,

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.680
right?

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.680
>> Well, my first um

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.280
I guess exposure to business in general

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.920
was actually working with my working

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.680
with my granddad. He would tell me, just

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.040
as we were working away, about how he

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.440
started his business. And he would tell

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.720
me about all the risks that he had to

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.280
took. And that was a really important

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.360
thing for me because one, it really

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.120
taught me work ethic, but secondly, it

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.280
also taught me that every business has

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.960
risk. And you going to have to get used

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.880
to and comfortable with taking that risk

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.200
cuz it's not, you know, it's not a

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.920
you can't win every time, right? When I

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.160
was at school, then got into app

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.800
development, web development, and

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.640
actually I guess led by a neighbor of

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.120
ours at the time, started selling number

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.560
plates online. After that, I got into

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.120
app development, so I made a couple of

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.720
iPhone uh sorry, three or four iPhone

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.880
apps. And then, I think I was about 18,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:20.160
19. I felt like I'd made lots of free

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.960
things and I wanted to make something

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.200
that would sell things online. And all I

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.560
knew is I wanted something to I want to

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.240
sell something online and I want it to

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.040
be in fitness. And basically bought the

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.920
gymshark.co.uk domain. It was £3.50 off

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.240
GoDaddy. Tied it into a Shopify store

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.320
and started drop shipping products from

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.000
there. It was actually supplements at

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.680
the time. That's how Gymshark was born.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.280
It was off the back of number plates

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.520
online, iPhone apps, fitness forums. And

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.800
I think in my experience is the first

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.960
thing you start is almost never going to

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.480
be the thing that you end up on. And

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.960
it's almost never successful. It's

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.480
almost like um

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.200
playing your first game of football and

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.560
then thinking you're going to be a

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.680
footballer by the end of it. You know

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.080
what I mean? You have to play, you have

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.400
to win, you have to lose, you have to

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.000
learn, you have to iterate. You might

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.240
try something. You might then find out

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.600
that you don't enjoy it, you want to try

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.280
something else. These are all the sort

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.920
of things that I think that I mean, the

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.320
earlier that you learn it, the better. I

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.720
think the secret sauce of your business

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.080
isn't just a great product.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.320
>> Yeah.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.760
>> I actually think it's that almost niche

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.360
that you picked where you said, "I like

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.520
going to the gym." You solved a problem

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.880
for yourself personally.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:16.800
>> Yeah.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.360
>> You knew that problem intimately that

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.000
most of the gym stuff was for people

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.160
with big muscles and that kind of whole

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.760
golden gym model. And and you were

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.040
solving a pain problem for yourself.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.760
>> Yeah.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.920
>> I think that's the the thing is cuz I'm

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.560
now looking at business from a different

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.959
perspective, right? We're 12, 13 years

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.200
in. I feel like I've been doing this for

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:33.959
a long time, and I want to do it for a

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.080
lot longer. Then it's even more

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:37.520
important that you're passionate about

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:39.480
what you do because it takes such a

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.920
level of dedication, patience, and

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:42.160
resilience to continue to build a

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:44.120
business for the long term. Like,

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.760
running a business for a year is hard

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.320
work. Running it for 2 years is slightly

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:49.480
harder work. When you get into 5, 10,

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.720
15, 20 years, it's very, very difficult

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.880
because you've got to remain so

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.280
consistent and so dedicated. You need to

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.040
build something that

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.320
you can be the best in the world at. If

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.720
you just love fishing, fishing is your

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.360
thing, you've done it since you're a

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.239
kid, and you just obsess over it, and

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.800
you know the details that anyone else

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:07.640
who's just doing it for the money won't

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:09.519
know. That's where you can win because

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:10.880
your edge is your knowledge and it's

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:13.120
your passion, and it's your focus. And I

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.320
think if you can use that rather than

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.480
looking at fundamentals like margin or

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.040
price point or your point, "What's going

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.120
to make me the most money?" I think I

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.400
think that's where people should be

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.959
focusing. And again, I think it's just

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.560
so important that kids learn this early

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:27.239
because those are the sort of um mental

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.320
frameworks that I think a lot of kids

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:31.000
don't have, and a lot of kids will maybe

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.760
build up the courage to start a business

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.120
and then fail and then think, "Oh, this

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:35.600
isn't for me." But that it might not

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.720
necessarily be the case. Or and I know a

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.840
lot of people that have done this. They

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.680
wanted to start a business when they

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.040
were a teenager. They just didn't then

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.680
quite build up the courage, and now

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.519
they're leaving their full-time jobs to

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.200
try it now, regretting the fact that

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:46.800
they didn't do it 10, 15 years ago.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.560
>> True.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:50.040
>> You weren't really thinking about making

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.400
huge amounts of money in the beginning.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.240
Your aim was not to be a billionaire,

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.000
right? Your aim was to solve problem

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.680
that you felt you had when going to the

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.280
gym. And I think this is a message I

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:59.600
kind of want to hammer home to people.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.040
Could you give your own interpretation?

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.120
>> My view on this, I've got a really clear

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.360
view. I think the best thing any young

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.120
entrepreneur can do is set the bar

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.040
overwhelmingly low. And what I mean by

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.600
that is like the day one goal for me

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.440
was, like I said, make a fitness website

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.800
that would transact. It wasn't to make a

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.200
multi-billion dollar business. It wasn't

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.720
to sell globally. It wasn't even to make

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:20.120
a certain product. It was fitness

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.320
transact. Then it was sell a product.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.120
And then it took us a couple of months.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.400
We sold a product. Then it was sell a

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:26.160
product a month. And then it's a product

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.520
a week. And then it's Okay, well, we're

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.760
selling regularly, but the margin's not

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.320
where we want. We need a higher margin

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.240
product. Okay, let's make a t-shirt, a

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.800
hoodie, shorts. What we never did was

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:36.400
then when it We want to do this massive

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.560
huge thing. And I think that was in the

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.520
back of our minds, right? It's There's a

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:41.160
dream in the back of your mind. But

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:42.960
practically, I think setting the bar low

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.000
is really important. Then for any young

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.520
entrepreneur that's building their

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.240
business, it's like every day can feel

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.840
like a win. And that That's how I would

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.440
see it. And I think just one step at a

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.560
time, one focus at a time. And then

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.880
eventually after a year or two, you'll

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:54.520
sort of you'll look over your shoulder

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.600
and you'll you'll be able to recognize

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:56.960
how far you've come. I think

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.000
relationship is another thing that a lot

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:00.240
of people overlook. I I I One of the

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.680
things I'm proud of over the last 25

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:03.440
years is I've never screwed anyone.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:05.480
You'll never find anyone that I have

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.680
done bad to. Yeah, it's not to say that

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.080
everyone will always agree with the

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.560
decisions that you make. But I think if

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.200
you can focus on making them in the

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:13.240
right way, communicating in the right

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.040
way, I think again business is so much

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.960
based on partnerships. Whether it's the

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.680
people that you directly work with or in

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.720
our case it's manufacturing partners

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.919
that we work with. And we've worked

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.560
with, you know, all of our biggest

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.600
partners for a long, long time now. And

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.040
there's a there's a really strong level

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.680
of trust there. And I think that again

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.760
that's really, really, really important.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.680
I actually think the biggest asset you

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:32.080
can ever have is industry respect. Where

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.440
people know they shake your hand and a

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:35.160
deal is done. And I don't think that's

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.400
promoted enough as a as a narrative in

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.960
business. It's all about like it's still

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.160
a little bit 1980s, you know, greed is

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:42.440
good. That's a narrative pushed online.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:44.160
But the reality is that I've seen people

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.080
that are really famous on the internet

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.720
lose out on massive life-changing

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.640
opportunities because of their personal

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:52.000
brand reputation. Again, for anyone

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:54.320
watching, the simple way I would think

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.880
about it is if you've got two options,

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.200
generally you will go with the person

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:59.480
that you trust the most or you think is

00:05:57.200 --> 00:06:01.520
genuinely going to be there for you when

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:03.000
you need them. And I think when it's not

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.480
to say that you don't have contracts and

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.360
you don't protect yourself legally, but

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.640
nine times out of 10, if you're checking

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.640
against a contract, you're not doing it

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.720
because things are going really, really

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.360
well, right? You're not going, "Oh, this

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.560
is going so wonderfully well. Let me see

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.400
how the contract is." It's because

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:16.520
things aren't going well. So, I think

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.240
you're right. I think trust in business

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.960
and being true to your word and honest

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.720
and making the tough decisions but in

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:24.960
the right way, it's um

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.480
it's definitely the right way to run a

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.640
business. When you think about, let's

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:30.320
say, diversification, of course you

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:32.240
probably think about it within clothing

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.680
ranges, but do you think about it from,

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.840
say for example, opening up your own

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.040
gym? So, there's two ways that we've

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.840
considered building our business out.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.280
There's the first way, which I would

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.120
probably describe as more conventional,

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.080
which is what can we do more of that is

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.720
almost aligned to or adjacent with what

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.280
we currently do. So, a real obvious

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:51.000
example for us, so we only currently

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.120
focus on building product for the gym.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.520
It would be very easy for us to go,

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.520
"Right, we're going to do fashion

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:57.200
because it's the same supply chain. We

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:58.680
can use a lot of the same infrastructure

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.880
that we've built, and we can stretch the

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:02.720
Gymshark brand into somewhere that

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.640
commercially and operationally is

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.200
similar, but also it's different enough

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.840
to help grow the business." The other

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.200
way, which is the way that certainly I

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.800
and we favor, is what makes the most

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:15.360
sense as a customer to our community and

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:17.000
to the brand first, regardless of how

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.160
operationally complex it is. So, what I

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.400
don't want to do is go, "Oh, this is

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.240
easy, so this is the right thing to do."

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.600
I want to go, "What feels right and what

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:24.040
is right?" And that's what we'll focus

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:26.040
on doing. So, gym is actually one of

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:27.440
those things. Operationally is very

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.840
different, right? Running a gym, selling

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.360
clothing, they're two completely

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.280
different things. But as a customer of

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:34.480
Gymshark, the biggest producer of

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:35.600
gymwear, the gym makes complete sense.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.720
And that's exactly what we're looking

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.440
at. We're looking at building a gym that

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:42.480
is iconic and special and unique. And

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:45.000
you know, the the physical manifestation

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.680
of not only the Gymshark brand, but the

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.720
Gymshark product and the Gymshark

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:51.560
community. Gymshark was built

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.920
essentially in my image, a young teenage

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.960
guy that wanted to lift weights and you

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.720
know, want to do well in the gym,

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.400
basically. And I'm really proud of that

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.800
because that that's what gave Gymshark

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.240
its start. But now Gymshark is so much

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.880
more than that, right? So, after that we

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.720
went into women's and we built out a

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.120
larger product portfolio and so on. What

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.000
we've done is we've gone from just being

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:10.200
a men's lifting brand to being a men's

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.720
and women's gym brand.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.240
>> We're running the world's biggest

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:16.200
business competition. We're giving up to

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:18.280
a million US dollars away and free help.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.919
